          }
        },
        "question_BtY6gg": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Why is aftercare important for piercings and jewellery?",
            "answer": "<p>Proper aftercare helps prevent irritation, promotes healing, and keeps your jewellery<br/>looking bright and clean. Using high-quality aftercare products ensures your piercings remain healthy and your jewellery maintains its shine over time.</p>",
            "icon": "none"
          }
        },
        "question_KUMeVf": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What types of aftercare products do you offer?",
            "answer": "<p>Our aftercare range includes:</p><ul><li><strong>Polishing kits</strong> – designed to safely clean and restore shine to your gold, silver, titanium, and steel jewellery.</li><li><strong>Coco balm</strong> – a natural moisturising balm that soothes and nourishes healed piercings.</li><li><strong>Tea tree oil spray</strong> – helps calm irritation and reduce redness around healed piercings.</li><li><strong>Jojoba healing oil</strong> – promotes hydration and supports skin recovery after piercing.</li></ul><p>Each product is carefully formulated for safe, effective use on body jewellery and pierced skin.</p>",
            "icon": "none"
          }
        },
        "question_RYdfWg": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How do I use your polishing kits?",
            "answer": "<p>Our polishing kits include specialised cloths and cleaners designed for <strong>gold, silver, titanium, and steel jewellery</strong>. Gently polish the surface in small circular motions to restore shine — do not use on raw skin or fresh piercings. Avoid soaking jewellery in cleaning solutions.</p>",
            "icon": "none"
          }
        },
        "question_yyxfHK": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What’s the difference between jojoba oil and tea tree oil spray?",
            "answer": "<ul><li><strong>Jojoba oil</strong> is deeply moisturising and helps maintain skin elasticity around the piercing. It’s gentle enough for sensitive skin and promotes natural healing.</li><li><strong>Tea tree oil spray</strong> is antimicrobial and soothing, ideal for reducing mild redness or irritation in healed or healing piercings.</li></ul><p>Both can be used as part of a gentle aftercare routine for skin and jewellery<br/>upkeep.</p>",
            "icon": "none"
          }
        },
        "question_kBHWxU": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Are your aftercare products natural and skin-safe?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes. Our aftercare range is made with <strong>natural, skin-safe ingredients</strong>, free from harsh chemicals or alcohol. They’re formulated to be gentle yet effective for daily piercing and jewellery maintenance.</p>",
            "icon": "none"
          }
        },
        "question_Ww86FC": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Can I use coco balm on fresh piercings?",
            "answer": "<p>Coco balm is best for <strong>healed piercings</strong>. It nourishes dry or stretched skin and adds shine to healed areas but should not be applied to fresh piercings, as heavy balms can block airflow and slow healing.</p>",
            "icon": "none"
          }
        },
        "question_iKhpNQ": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Do you offer wholesale pricing for aftercare products?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes. We supply our full range of <strong>aftercare products, including oils, sprays, and polishing kits</strong>, at wholesale rates for studios and retailers. Log in or contact our wholesale<br/>team for trade pricing and stock details.</p>",
            "icon": "none"
          }
        }
